{
  "abstract": "An independent Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the theorem of Liam Kruer and Jensen Kohlmeyer (2026) resolving both parts of Erdős Problem 14. For every A subset N and every N >= 2 * 10000^4, the number of integers in {1, ..., N} not uniquely representable as an unordered sum of two elements of A is at least sqrt(N) / 6000. This establishes Part (i) (nonUniqueSumCount A >> N^(1/2 - eps) for all eps > 0) and refutes the Part (ii) question (no A has nonUniqueSumCount A = o(sqrt(N))). The compared declarations in `Challenge.lean` match `FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/14.lean` for Part (i) and state the exact negation of the open existential question for Part (ii).",
  "authors": [
